<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two S.Korean firms buy 22,500T of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Two S.Korean firms buy 22,500T of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheiljedang Corp and Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd on Friday bought a total of 22,500 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat from Japanese trading house Nichimen Corp, traders said.  </p>
<p>Cheiljedang had initially invited tenders for 7,000 tonnes at basis over May futures on the U.S grain futures markets including the Chicago Board of Trade, but they bought the wheat at fixed prices, traders said.</p>
<p>Dongah Flour also bought the remaining 15,500 tonnes at fixed prices.</p>
<p>Shipment was set for April 10-May 10 to the port of Pusan.</p>
<p>Details for the results are as follows:</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/Tonne(FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		6,900   $154.75</p>
<p>(protein max 10.0%)</p>
<p>  Western White	   1,000   $155.50</p>
<p>(club wheat minimum 15%)</p>
<p>  Soft White		1,100   $154.75</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 7,200   $181.50</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  6,300   $186.30</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
